.TH FREEMIC 1 "2026-10-30" "FreeMic 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
freemic \- soundboard and virtual microphone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freemic
[\fB\-\-minimized\fR]
.br
.B freemic
\fB\-\-play\fR \fINAME\fR|\fB#\fR\fIN\fR | \fB\-\-stop\fR | \fB\-\-quit\fR
.br
.B freemic
\fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
FreeMic mixes your microphone with sound clips from a button grid and sends
the result to a virtual microphone named
.B "FreeMic Virtual Microphone"
that other programs (voice chat, games, recording software) can select.
The virtual microphone is created through PulseAudio or PipeWire
(pipewire-pulse) while FreeMic runs and is removed when it exits.
FreeMic never changes the default input or output device and plays nothing
to your speakers unless monitoring is enabled in its settings.
.PP
The YouTube page saves the audio of single YouTube videos into the sound
library. It uses yt-dlp, which FreeMic downloads from yt-dlp's GitHub
releases on first use and verifies against the published SHA-256 sums.
Playlists are never downloaded.
.PP
Without options FreeMic opens its window. Only one instance runs per user;
the command options below control the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start with the window minimized.
.TP
.BI \-\-play " NAME" "\fR|\fP#" N
Play the sound called \fINAME\fR (case-insensitive), or the \fIN\fRth button.
If that sound is already playing it is stopped. Useful for keyboard shortcuts
on Wayland, where applications cannot register global hotkeys.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the soundboard (the microphone keeps working).
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Close the running FreeMic.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help text.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if FreeMic is not running or the sound was not found.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/freemic/
settings.json and soundboard.json.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/freemic/
Imported sounds (sounds/), YouTube audio (sounds/youtube/), yt-dlp (tools/)
and the log file freemic.log.
.TP
.I portable.txt
If this file (or a data directory) exists next to the program, all data is
kept in the data directory there instead.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FREEMIC_STATS=1
Log microphone buffer and drift statistics (for bug reports).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR pavucontrol (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/freemic/
